{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487321814,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMDgzNzYzNjA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1311","origin":"github"},"title":"New re-used repo dataset/repo instances need different invalidation logic","message":"Here is the demo\n\n````\n\u003e\u003e\u003e from datalad.api import create\n\u003e\u003e\u003e ds = create('here')\n\u003e\u003e\u003e ds.remove()\n\u003e\u003e\u003e ds = create('here')\n[INFO] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/bugdemo/here \n[ERROR] Failed to run ['git', 'config', '--file', '/tmp/bugdemo/here/.datalad/config', '--unset-all', 'datalad.dataset.id'] under '/tmp/bugdemo/here'. Exit code=5. out= err= \n````\n\nReason is: in `create` it unsets config variables if they are present. The config of the removed dataset is still loaded in the cfg manager of that dataset, but there is nothing in the actual config file, hence `git config` fails.","files":null}]}